---
import '../styles/global.css';

const nav = ['Work', 'Reading', 'Making', 'Notes', 'About'];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Inês Pinheiro is a senior data scientist who works on machine learning systems and makes things with code, yarn and paint." />
    <title>Inês Pinheiro</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wdth,wght@75..125,100..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header shell">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">Inês Pinheiro</a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        {nav.map((item) => <a href={`/#${item.toLowerCase()}`}>{item}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero shell">
        <div class="eyebrow">Senior data scientist · maker · reader</div>
        <h1>I work with <span>data, code</span> & machine learning.</h1>
        <div class="hero-aside">
          <div class="pattern" aria-hidden="true">× · × · · ×<br />· × · × × ·<br />× · · × · ×</div>
          <p>I also make things with yarn, pigment, paper and too many browser tabs.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="intro">I like work where the details matter: unreliable models, awkward inputs, concurrent systems and tools people need to trust.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="currently shell" id="now">
        <div class="section-index">01 / currently</div>
        <div class="current-lead">
          <p class="scribble">on my desk</p>
          <h2>Things I’m spending time on now.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="current-grid">
          <article><span>Reading</span><h3>A small stack, always changing</h3><a href="#reading">See the reading list ↗</a></article>
          <article><span>Building</span><h3>A commonplace book made for the way I think</h3><p>A personal tool for collecting what I read, making connections and finding it again later.</p></article>
          <article><span>Making</span><h3>With yarn, watercolour and code</h3><a href="#making">Things I make ↗</a></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="work shell" id="work">
        <div class="section-index">02 / selected work</div>
        <div class="work-heading"><h2>Problems I’ve spent time thinking about.</h2><p>I lead small data science and machine learning teams from an untidy brief through architecture, experiments, code review and delivery.</p></div>
        <article class="case-study">
          <div class="case-number">01</div>
          <div><div class="tags">LLMs / NLP / system design</div><h3>Can an LLM summary earn an editor’s trust?</h3><p>Long-form book summarisation where no single validator gets the last word. Genre routing, source-grounded entities, claim-level judging and deterministic checks catch different kinds of failure.</p></div>
          <a href="#">Case study soon ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="case-study">
          <div class="case-number">02</div>
          <div><div class="tags">NLP / analytics / production ML</div><h3>What happens when an ML product outgrows the system it started with?</h3><p>I built the first Reviews Radar pipeline, then later led its redesign when a data-source migration pushed each refresh from thousands of rows to millions. The new system changed the data path, the LLM stack and the topic model rather than stretching the old design past its limits.</p></div>
          <a href="#">Case study soon ↗</a>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="reading" id="reading">
        <div class="shell reading-inner">
          <div class="section-index">03 / reading · 2026</div>
          <div class="reading-number">2026</div>
          <div class="reading-copy"><h2>What I’ve been reading.</h2><p>Fiction, essays, technical rabbit holes and the books that follow me around after I’ve put them down.</p><a href="#">Open the shelf ↗</a></div>
          <div class="mini-books" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="making shell" id="making">
        <div class="section-index">04 / making</div>
        <h2>Sometimes with code.<br /><span>Sometimes with my hands.</span></h2>
        <div class="making-grid">
          <div class="art art-yarn"><span>knitting / in progress</span><div class="stitches">∨ ∨ ∨ ∨ ∨<br />∨ ∧ ∨ ∧ ∨<br />∧ ∨ ∧ ∨ ∧</div></div>
          <div class="art art-paint"><span>watercolour / studies</span><div class="wash"></div></div>
          <div class="art art-code"><span>software / commonplace</span><strong>COMMON<br />PLACE</strong><small>a personal knowledge system built around how I want to use it</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="shell" id="about"><div>Inês Pinheiro · 2026</div><div>Designed, coded & occasionally unravelled.</div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
